The state Department of Education invites the public to review proposed instructional materials for South Carolina's public schools. This virtual review covers three programs that districts have requested for evaluation and possible state adoption. The board's Instructional Materials Review Panel will submit its recommendations on these materials to the state Board of Education in January and February 2018.

The three district-requested programs are:
- Chinese Language Arts and Literacy Immersion Program, K-8; Publisher: Better Chinese; Program: Better Immersion Classroom Set, Levels S and 1-8;
- French, 6-12; Publisher: Houghton Mifflin Harcourt; Program: D'accord!;
- Spanish, 6-12; Publisher: National Geographic and Cengage Learning; Program: Exploremos!

The public can access these three programs digitally from December 11, 2017, through January 9, 2018. Publisher-provided links to the materials and a link to the form for submitting public comments are available online at goo.gl/d6NCo3.

