Company momentum continues with the winning of large enterprise deals and the launch of an innovative continuous testing solution.  
ATLANTA, GA--(Marketwired - Apr 18, 2017) - QASymphony, the leading provider of agile testing solutions to the Global 2000, kicks off its annual Quality Jam software testing conference today, with over 400 customers and partners in attendance. The event will feature top thought leaders in software testing, including Keith Klain, Michael Bolton, Paul Merrill, and many others.  
Quality Jam follows another successful quarter for QASymphony, which saw record revenue and major competitive wins. Below are some highlights from the quarter:  
120% year-over-year revenue growth;  
47 new customers added, including Global 2000 enterprises such as Citrix, Republic Services, Thomas Cook, and Omron;  
major expansion deals closed with Brown Brothers Harriman, Cisco, and FICO;  
the launch of qTest Pulse, a new solution focused on continuous testing with integrations to GitHub and other DevOps tools;  
the opening of a London office and the hiring of Bas Nijjer as General Manager of EMEA;  
and key executive additions: Guy Lever as VP of Customer Success and Eric Browning as VP of Security.  
"We are thrilled to celebrate our success with our customers and partners at Quality Jam this year. In Q1 we significantly exceeded expectations and positioned our company for continued long-term growth," said Dave Keil, CEO of QASymphony. "We are seeing increased demand among the Global 2000 for modern agile solutions that help improve software quality and gain a competitive advantage. The recent 'spin-merge' between HPE and MicroFocus has created more urgency for Quality Center customers to find alternative solutions. We are the only company offering a comprehensive testing and business intelligence platform that serves the different segments of the market."  
About QASymphony:  
QASymphony is a leading agile software company providing enterprise test case management and exploratory testing solutions for development and QA teams. The qTest Platform helps companies create better software by improving speed, efficiency, collaboration, and analysis during testing. The company has over 400 customers across 20 countries, including Salesforce, Barclays, Adobe, Samsung, Verizon, and Office Depot. QASymphony was recently selected by Gartner as a "Cool Vendor in Application Development" and by Entrepreneur Magazine as one of the "Best Entrepreneurial Companies in America." The company is headquartered in Atlanta, GA. To learn more, visit www.qasymphony.com or follow on Twitter at @QASymphony.
